{"repositoryId":286775935,"availability":"available","full":"Blues1998/Blues1998.github.io","name":"Blues1998.github.io","description":"My personal site: an Astro portfolio that renders every page over one persistent three.js scene, so navigating is a camera move rather than a page load.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2020-08-11T15:09:50Z","updated":"2026-09-02T23:53:29Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://blues1998.github.io","topics":["astro","personal-website","portfolio","three-js","typescript","webgl"],"demo":"https://blues1998.github.io/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T07:15:31.520Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T07:15:31.520Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T07:15:31.520Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T07:15:31.520Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Three.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Personal site of Animesh Singh — software engineer, photographer, and musician. Live at blues1998.github.io.","It is a static Astro site, but not a document with a background: every page renders over one persistent WebGL scene. Six destinations map to six astronomical objects, and navigating between them is a camera move toward the next one rather than a page load — the same canvas, the same camera, carried across navigations by Astro's view transitions."],"features":["A persistent three.js cosmos. A layered procedural starfield, a","planetary system, a pulsar, a galaxy and a nebula built as GPU point clouds, plus real scanned NASA/JAXA geometry (the Itokawa asteroid, a Voyager probe) and NASA-derived planet textures.","Scroll as camera movement. On inner pages, sections are stations","along an approach: the camera closes and orbits as you read, so reading a page is travelling toward its object.","An interactive playground. Wander is an endless procedural scenic"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Blues1998/Blues1998.github.io/blob/main/README.md","fingerprin